---
source: crates/cache-explorer-core/tests/golden.rs
description: "Frame 3b's accesses as in frame-3b-accesses, timed 1/20: each miss stalls once its victim is chosen, and the dirty eviction stalls for 40 cycles, 20 for the write-back and 20 for the fill. Cycles are charged where the time is spent, so the write-back row reads 85 and the fill 105, rather than the whole miss at the Miss row (cases 7, 2, 7, 1 and 4)."
---
1.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 0 | Store 0x0B0: tag 0x02, set 3, offset 0 (word 0).
1.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, cycles, compulsory | 1 | Set 3: no valid way holds tag 0x02. Miss.
1.3 | victim | associativity | - | 1 | Way 0 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
1.4 | stall | timing | - | 1 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while memory supplies line 0x0B0.
1.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 3/0, tag 3/0, word 3/0/0, word 3/0/1, word 3/0/2, word 3/0/3, fills, cycles | 21 | Fill way 0 with line 0x0B0–0x0BF from memory.
1.6 | write | writePolicy | dirty 3/0, word 3/0/0 | 21 | Write 5 into word 0 of way 0 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x0B0 is now stale.
2.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 21 | Load 0x0A4: tag 0x02, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
2.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, cycles, compulsory | 22 | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x02. Miss.
2.3 | victim | associativity | - | 22 | Way 0 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
2.4 | stall | timing | - | 22 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while memory supplies line 0x0A0.
2.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/0, tag 2/0, word 2/0/0, word 2/0/1, word 2/0/2, word 2/0/3, fills, cycles | 42 | Fill way 0 with line 0x0A0–0x0AF from memory.
2.6 | complete | - | r1 | 42 | Read word 1 of way 0 (53) into r1.
3.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 42 | Store 0x1A4: tag 0x06, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
3.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, stores, misses, cycles, compulsory | 43 | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x06. Miss.
3.3 | victim | associativity | - | 43 | Way 1 chosen: it is invalid (empty).
3.4 | stall | timing | - | 43 | The CPU stalls for 20 cycles while memory supplies line 0x1A0.
3.5 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, fills, cycles | 63 | Fill way 1 with line 0x1A0–0x1AF from memory.
3.6 | write | writePolicy | dirty 2/1, word 2/1/1 | 63 | Write 7 into word 1 of way 1 and set its dirty bit. Memory at 0x1A4 is now stale.
3.7 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1 | 63 | LRU ranks in set 2: way 1 becomes 0 (most recent); way 0 is 1.
4.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 63 | Load 0x0A8: tag 0x02, set 2, offset 8 (word 2).
4.2 | hit | associativity | accesses, loads, hits, cycles | 64 | Set 2, way 0: valid, and tag 0x02 matches. Hit.
4.3 | complete | - | r1 | 64 | Read word 2 of way 0 (66) into r1.
4.4 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1 | 64 | LRU ranks in set 2: way 0 becomes 0 (most recent); way 1 is 1.
5.1 | decode | lineSize | - | 64 | Load 0x2A4: tag 0x0A, set 2, offset 4 (word 1).
5.2 | miss | associativity | accesses, loads, misses, cycles, compulsory | 65 | Set 2: no valid way holds tag 0x0A. Miss.
5.3 | victim | replacement | - | 65 | Way 1 chosen: least recently used (rank 1).
5.4 | stall | timing | - | 65 | The CPU stalls for 40 cycles: 20 to write line 0x1A0 back, then 20 to fetch line 0x2A0.
5.5 | writeBack | writePolicy | memory 0x1A4, writebacks, cycles | 85 | Way 1 is dirty: write line 0x1A0 back to memory first.
5.6 | evict | replacement | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, dirty 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, evictions | 85 | Evict line 0x1A0 (tag 0x06) from way 1.
5.7 | fill | lineSize | valid 2/1, tag 2/1, word 2/1/0, word 2/1/1, word 2/1/2, word 2/1/3, fills, cycles | 105 | Fill way 1 with line 0x2A0–0x2AF from memory.
5.8 | complete | - | r1 | 105 | Read word 1 of way 1 (68) into r1.
5.9 | rank | replacement | rank 2/0, rank 2/1 | 105 | LRU ranks in set 2: way 1 becomes 0 (most recent); way 0 is 1.
